<title>GREECE: Greek/Bund gap shrinks to 357 bps, 252 vs BTP.</title>
<headline>Greek/Bund gap shrinks to 357 bps, 252 vs BTP.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The spread of Greece's 10-year bond over bunds was trimmed to 357 basis points from 359 on Friday.</p>
<p>The Greek/BTP gap also fell to 252 basis points from 258 on Friday.</p>
<p>		 CPN     MATURITY  YIELDS    SPREADS    PREVIOUS</p>
<p>								    SPREADS</p>
<p>   GREECE    8.80%   25JUN07    9.15%</p>
<p>   GERMANY   6.0%    04JUL07    5.58%	357	359 bps</p>
<p>   FRANCE    5.5%    25APR07    5.48%	367	372 bps</p>
<p>   ITALY     6.75%   01FEB07    6.63%	252	258 bps</p>
<p>   PORTUGAL  6.63%   23FEB07    6.33%	282	287 bps</p>
<p>   SPAIN     7.35%   31MAR07    6.27%	288	293 bps</p>
<p>   UK	  7.25%   07DEC07    7.14%	201	206 bps</p>
<p>   US	  6.63%   15MAY07    6.39%	276	279 bps</p>
<p>All yields are annualised and based on bid prices at 0930 GMT.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
